    <!-- Section 1: Agile -->
    <h2 class="text-success">What is Agile?</h2>
    <p>
        Agile is a project management and software development methodology that emphasizes flexibility, collaboration, and customer satisfaction.
        It follows an iterative approach where teams work in short cycles called **sprints** to develop and improve software continuously.
    </p>

    <h3>Key Agile Principles:</h3>
    <ul class="list-group">
        <li class="list-group-item">Customer satisfaction through early and continuous delivery.</li>
        <li class="list-group-item">Welcome changing requirements, even in late development stages.</li>
        <li class="list-group-item">Deliver working software frequently (weeks rather than months).</li>
        <li class="list-group-item">Collaboration between developers and business teams.</li>
        <li class="list-group-item">Motivated individuals and self-organizing teams.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="text-center">
        <img src="~/images/agile-methodology.png" alt="Agile Methodology" class="img-fluid rounded mt-3" width="60%">
        <p class="text-muted">Figure: Agile Methodology Workflow</p>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <!-- Section 2: Azure Dashboard -->
    <h2 class="text-primary">What is Azure Dashboard?</h2>
    <p>
        The Azure DevOps Dashboard is a project management tool used to track software development progress, manage work items, and collaborate effectively.
    </p>

    <h3>Azure DevOps Features:</h3>
    <ul class="list-group">
        <li class="list-group-item">**Boards** - Used for project planning, tracking Epics, Tasks, and Issues.</li>
        <li class="list-group-item">**Repos** - Git repositories for source code management.</li>
        <li class="list-group-item">**Pipelines** - Continuous Integration and Deployment (CI/CD).</li>
        <li class="list-group-item">**Test Plans** - Manual and automated testing.</li>
        <li class="list-group-item">**Artifacts** - Package management.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="text-center">
        <img src="~/images/azure-dashboard.png" alt="Azure Dashboard" class="img-fluid rounded mt-3" width="60%">
        <p class="text-muted">Figure: Azure DevOps Dashboard</p>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <h3>Example of Epics, Tasks, and Issues</h3>
    <p>
        In Azure DevOps, work items are managed using a hierarchy:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>**Epic** - Large features that require multiple sprints.</li>
        <li>**Feature** - A subset of an epic, representing a specific functionality.</li>
        <li>**Task** - A smaller, actionable item within a feature.</li>
        <li>**Issue** - A problem or bug that needs to be resolved.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="text-center">
        <img src="~/Images\AzureDevops\AzureAgileWOrkFlow.png" alt="Azure Work Items Example" class="img-fluid rounded mt-3" width="60%">
        <p class="text-muted">Figure: Work Item Hierarchy in Azure DevOps</p>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <h2 class="text-success">Conclusion</h2>
    <p>
        Understanding Agile methodology and Azure DevOps Dashboard is essential for modern software development.
        Agile ensures continuous improvement, while Azure DevOps helps track progress and manage projects efficiently.
    </p>
